# What `docker build -f app/Dockerfile app` must NOT upload as build context
# (app/cloudbuild.yaml builds with `app` as the context, so THIS file governs it
# — the repo-root .dockerignore covers the API build, whose context is `.`).
#
# Until this file existed, `COPY . .` in the builder stage carried a local
# `node_modules` and a local `dist` into the image layer, only for `npm ci` and
# `npm run build` to overwrite both. Worse, it carried anything named `.env`:
# the app's dev file holds VITE_ADMIN_TOKEN, and a build arg is not needed for a
# secret to end up in a layer — being in the context is enough.
#
# Everything the build genuinely needs stays: index.html, src/, public/,
# scripts/, prerender/ (the prebuild step rewrites it), the tsconfig/vite/eslint
# configs, package.json + package-lock.json, and the three nginx files the
# runtime stage copies (nginx.conf, security-headers.conf and the origin gate's
# origin-gate.conf.template).

# Installed and generated by the build itself
node_modules
dist
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# Never in a layer. `.env*` on purpose, not the three named files: the app's
# .env carries VITE_ADMIN_TOKEN, and a variant nobody thought of (.env.staging)
# is exactly how the next one gets in.
.env*

# Noise
.gitignore
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
